; Gauntlet program 5 — formatted output.
;
; The only gauntlet program with an effect. Three things are tested at once:
;
;   1. A host binding costs nothing. `print-line` is one line in targets/*.oro
;      and no Go — g5's claim that an extern is a vocabulary entry.
;   2. Order survives reduction. The three lines must print in the order
;      written, once each, however aggressively β rewrites around them.
;   3. A pure computation feeds an effectful call. `dot` is now imported from
;      num/vec rather than repeated here, and must still fuse into one loop
;      with no intermediate vector.
;
; The last one is the interesting case: an effect must not block fusion in the
; pure part, and a fused pure part must not move the effect.

(use num/vec)

; `seq` is sugar for nested applications with an ignored binder, and it survives
; reduction only because β refuses to drop an impure argument that is used zero
; times — effects.md §5.
(fn (label xs)
  (seq (print-line label)
       (print-line (alen xs))
       (print-line (vec.dot xs xs))))
